	I have been seeing quite a few posts about hackers getting killed
by the wizard after getting the amulet. I was a little surprised, because
to date the wizard has never killed me( I've had about 10 games where I've
gotten the amulet). Of those 10 times, I finished 5 times and was killed by 
stupid deaths the rest of the time. I don't know if many of you do what I 
am going to suggest, but it always works for me.












Minor Spoiler

I always make sure I have more than one way to level teleport before I go
to Hell. It may be either 2 cursed scrolls of teleportation, 2 level teleport
traps etc. I also make sure I have intrinsic teleportation and teleport 
control. I think after a certain amount of time after you gain intrinsic 
random teleportation, it becomes controllable. My guess is that it varies 
with the characters intelligence.
Once I have these, I go down to Level 50 and come all the way back up to the
Medusa level, WITHOUT KILLING THE WIZARD AND GETTING THE AMULET. This way
the next time you can level teleport down to the level where the Wizard is,
kill him, grab the amulet and scoot back to the endlevel. It is much faster
and easier, because you know where all the exits (stairways) are, as you
already went through once. I basically teleport from stairway to stairway
in each level. The only problem is food. Carrying a bunch of rations and
scattering foodrations at intermediate levels will solve the problem.

I have always used this method, and have never had to face the wizard more
than twice, with the second time being in the endlevel.If you also have
a ring of conflict, you can breeze through the endlevel easily. THe last
time I had a ring of conflict, I did not face the Wizard again, after killing
him the first time.

As far as I know, there is no sure way to make sure that the Wizard won't
come back.l prefer to use the above method.

Anyone have a different method???







